      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Stremsgallery",
      "description": "The photograph, taken by Valeria Beltrán at the Monastery of Santa María de la Murta (Alzira, Valencia), captures the essence of a historic and spiritual site nestled in nature. This place, part of the well-known Monastery Route, conveys serenity, silence, and the feeling that time stands still.\nBeltrán, a landscape and conceptual photographer, seeks in this work a direct connection between the viewer and the environment portrayed. Using a Nikon D5500 camera with a tripod, she carefully crafted the composition. Post-editing was minimal, limited to a slight lighting adjustment, reinforcing her commitment to an honest and faithful aesthetic.\n\nThe frame reflects not only the beauty of the landscape but also the mystical, almost sacred atmosphere of the site. Light, textures, and composition invite the viewer to contemplate the scene without artifices, revealing nature and traces of the past in their most authentic state.",
